    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear mandate: exploit the soft matchups against pitchers like Littell, Kochanowicz, and Imai. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 87.14 score; despite the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time creating a marginal risk for his stolen base upside, the favorable park factors and high-leverage spot in the #2 hole make him our most potent asset. Following close behind is **Josh Naylor** (77.20) and **James Wood** (75.08), both of whom benefit from significant lineup order advantages and elite xwOBA projections. **Brice Turang** (73.40) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) round out our tier-one plays, with the former enjoying a substantial park boost that vaults him into must-start territory.\n\nWhile the optimizer remains aggressive, the decision to bench **Austin Riley** (46.73) was the most difficult choice on the board. Although he possesses high-upside power, his 3.32 xERA matchup against Ashcraft forced a drop below our efficiency threshold when measured against the lineup-position stability offered by players like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Alex Freeland**. Investors should keep a close eye on **Jose Caballero**, whose game has been flagged with a rainout status, removing him from consideration entirely. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the strikeout potential posed by Ryan facing **Vinnie Pasquantino**; while **Vinnie Pasquantino** holds a solid 57.84 score due to positive BvP trends, the SP skill gap suggests a volatile floor. All eyes remain on the leadoff production from **Cole Young** and **Travis Bazzana** to set the pace for an otherwise high-ceiling lineup.",
